\title{The Continued-Fraction Period of $\sqrt{N}$ as a Symmetric Channel:\\ Structure Without Leverage}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{14 August 2026}

\begin{abstract}
We give a complete integral analysis of the continued-fraction expansion of $\sqrt{N}$ regarded as an information channel from a composite integer $N$ to its factorization. Working entirely over $\Z$, we formulate the Lagrange (PQa) state machine as a six-coordinate recursion and establish its full set of conserved quantities: $d \mid N-m^{2}$, the linear relations $Nq = hm + h_{-}d$ and $qm + q_{-}d = h$, and unimodularity $(hq_{-}-h_{-}q)^{2}=1$. From these we deduce the exact norm identity $h^{2}-Nq^{2} = d\,(hq_{-}-h_{-}q) = \pm d$ at every convergent, hence that every state with $d=1$ produces a unit of $\Z[\sqrt N]$. We then determine the factoring leverage of the channel. Its unique factor-adjacent exit is the split-root event: a norm-$+1$ period-end unit is a square root of $1$ modulo $N$, and if split then $\gcd(x-1,N)$ is a proper divisor. Four obstructions close this exit: (i) odd prime powers are immune, since every square root of $1$ modulo $p^{k}$ is $\pm 1$; (ii) the cheap-period families $N=m^{2}+1$ and $N=m^{2}+2$ yield only trivial gcds, and for fixed denominator $y$ the number of $N \le X$ with a norm-$+1$ unit of that denominator is $O(y\sqrt X)$, hence density zero; (iii) all state coordinates are confined to the box $0 \le m \le \lfloor\sqrt N\rfloor$, $0 < d \le 2\lfloor\sqrt N\rfloor$ while convergent denominators satisfy $q_{k+1} \ge F_{k+1}$, so the cost is $\Theta(\ell(N))$ with empirical median $\ell/\sqrt N \approx 0.406$; (iv) the one genuine signal, period parity---equivalently solvability of $x^{2}-Ny^{2}=-1$, equivalently all odd prime factors $\equiv 1 \pmod 4$---is congruential, and by Dirichlet's theorem congruence data is compatible with infinitely many factorizations. Finally we dissolve an empirical confound: every partial quotient after the first is at most $2\lfloor\sqrt N\rfloor$, with equality exactly at period end, so the maximal partial quotient is identically the size coordinate $2\lfloor\sqrt N\rfloor$; after residualizing on $\lfloor\sqrt N\rfloor$, $120$ stratified permutation tests give worst $p=0.024$ against a Bonferroni threshold of $0.0004$. The barrier known for polynomial symmetric functions of the factors thus extends to the canonical non-polynomial symmetric $N$-computable object.
\end{abstract}

